# Git push policy

- Never run `git push` (or any command that publishes commits to a remote,
  e.g. `gh pr create` that pushes a branch) in this repository, under any
  circumstances, even if asked to "push", "publish", "sync", or "open a PR".
- If the user wants commits pushed, tell them the commits are ready locally
  and ask them to push. Do not push "just this once" even with explicit
  reassurance in the moment — always defer to the user running `git push`
  themselves.
- Local git operations (`git add`, `git commit`, `git status`, `git diff`,
  `git log`, local branches) are fine.
- Never add Cursor/AI attribution to commits or code: no "Co-Authored-By"
  trailers mentioning Cursor, no "Generated with Cursor" / "Made with
  Cursor" tags, badges, or comments in commit messages, README files, or
  source code.
